# Roadly — AI Agent Project Rules

## Project Context
- **Project:** Roadly — Customer Feedback & Public Roadmap SaaS
- **Stack:** MERN (MongoDB, Express.js, React, Node.js) + TypeScript
- **UI Library:** Coss UI (coss.com/ui) — MANDATORY, do not replace
- **Assessment:** Technical Assessment — Project 01 (Feature Request & Public Roadmap Portal)

## Critical Documentation
Before modifying ANY code, read the relevant docs from `docs/`:
- `00-PROJECT-MASTER.md` — Project overview, navigation, classification labels
- `01-REQUIREMENTS.md` — All 73 traced requirements (source: assessment PDFs)
- `05-API-SPECIFICATION.md` — Complete REST API reference
- `06-AUTH-SECURITY.md` — Auth architecture, token handling, cookie config
- `11-CODING-RULES.md` — Development standards
- `19-AI-AGENT-WORKFLOW.md` — Mandatory workflow steps

## Non-Negotiable Rules

### Security
1. **NEVER** store JWT access tokens in localStorage or sessionStorage
2. Access tokens live in React state/context (in-memory ONLY)
3. Refresh tokens are httpOnly cookies ONLY
4. All secrets via environment variables — never hardcoded
5. Authorization enforced at API level, not just frontend
6. Input validation on EVERY endpoint

### Architecture
7. Backend follows: Routes → Controllers → Services → Models
8. No business logic in routes or controllers
9. Centralized error handling via Express error middleware
10. Consistent response format: `{ success, data, error, meta }`
11. All UI components built on Coss UI primitives

### Code Quality
12. No unnecessary dependencies — justify each addition
13. No files exceeding ~300 lines; no components exceeding ~150 lines
14. No duplicate utilities — check existing code first
15. TypeScript strict mode — no `any` without justification
16. Meaningful names — no `data`, `temp`, `x`

### Process
17. Do NOT invent requirements — only implement what's in `01-REQUIREMENTS.md`
18. Do NOT modify unrelated files
19. Do NOT change architecture without updating `17-DECISION-LOG.md`
20. Do NOT mark tasks complete without testing
21. Update `18-PROGRESS-TRACKER.md` after completing tasks
22. Preserve existing behavior unless explicitly changing it

## Classification Labels
- 🔴 REQUIRED — From assessment PDFs, must implement
- 🟡 RECOMMENDED — Architecturally beneficial, proposed by docs
- 🔵 OPTIONAL — Nice-to-have, only after all REQUIRED features work
- ⚪ DEFERRED — Intentionally postponed
- 🟠 IMPLEMENTATION DECISION — Not specified, agent/dev decides

## Folder Structure Quick Reference
```
client/src/components/ui/       → Coss UI primitives (don't modify)
client/src/components/{feature}/ → Feature-specific components
client/src/pages/               → One component per route
client/src/hooks/               → Custom hooks
client/src/api/                 → API client functions
client/src/context/             → React Context (auth)
server/src/routes/              → Route definitions
server/src/controllers/         → Request/response handling
server/src/services/            → Business logic
server/src/models/              → Mongoose schemas
server/src/middleware/           → Auth, validation, errors
server/src/middleware/validations/ → Input validation schemas
```

## Key Technical Decisions
- Voting uses atomic MongoDB ops: `$addToSet`, `$pull`, `$inc` on embedded voters array
- Pagination: Offset-based with page numbers
- Comments: Adjacency list with 2-level max depth
- Validation: Zod in both apps; separate aligned schemas, server authoritative
- Server state: TanStack Query with optimistic updates for voting
- Auth: Dual JWT (access 15min in-memory + refresh 7d httpOnly cookie) with rotation
